# with an API key
claude mcp add --transport http my-app http://localhost:3000/mcp \
  --header "X-API-Key: &lt;key&gt;"
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "my-app": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://my-app.example.com/mcp"
    }
  }
}
</code></pre> <p><code>.vscode/mcp.json</code>:</p> <pre><code>{
  "servers": {
    "my-app": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "http://localhost:3000/mcp"
    }
  }
}
</code></pre> <p>The MCP Inspector is the best way to see exactly what your server exposes:</p> <pre><code>npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector
</code></pre> <p>Choose Streamable HTTP and enter <code>http://localhost:3000/mcp</code>.</p>
